<!-- Phase 5 website teaching layer; original chapter remains read-only. Evidence: website/reviews/android-phase5-findings.md. -->

<!-- @opening -->
<p class="story-lead">The scanner preview is smooth, but results describe where the barcode was a second ago. Throughput alone is misleading: the feature needs a recent frame and must return every borrowed image buffer.</p>

<!-- @after Analysis Pipeline :: animation -->
### Prefer a fresh answer over a growing queue

<figure class="stepper"><span class="stepper-title">KEEP_ONLY_LATEST while one frame is being analyzed</span><div class="stage viz-stack"><div class="node" data-el="analysis"><strong>Analyzer</strong><small data-text="analysisV">—</small></div><div class="node" data-el="latest"><strong>Waiting image</strong><small data-text="latestV">—</small></div><div class="node" data-el="result"><strong>Result</strong><small data-text="resultV">—</small></div></div><script type="application/json" class="steps">[
{
"label": "Analyze A",
"caption": "The analyzer owns frame A until it closes the ImageProxy.",
"state": {
"analysis": "active"
},
"text": {
"analysisV": "A in progress",
"latestV": "none",
"resultV": "pending"
},
"add": [
"analysis",
"latest",
"result"
]
},
{
"label": "New frames",
"caption": "B arrives, then C. The latest waiting image replaces older pending work.",
"state": {
"latest": "active"
},
"text": {
"latestV": "C replaces B"
}
},
{
"label": "Finish A",
"caption": "Finish using A, close its ImageProxy, then the next delivered image can be analyzed.",
"state": {
"analysis": "done",
"result": "active"
},
"text": {
"analysisV": "A closed",
"resultV": "A result"
}
},
{
"label": "Analyze latest",
"caption": "Continue with the latest waiting image rather than processing every stale intermediate frame.",
"state": {
"analysis": "active",
"latest": "done"
},
"text": {
"analysisV": "C in progress",
"latestV": "consumed"
}
}
]</script><figcaption>Close each ImageProxy on every completion path. For asynchronous inference, close after that work finishes using the image.</figcaption></figure>

<!-- @after Production Architecture :: check -->
### Try the decision

<details><summary>Preview works: analysis healthy?</summary>

Not necessarily. Preview can look smooth while the analyzer falls behind. Measure frame age, analyzer duration and dropped frames.
</details>

<details><summary>Close the wrapped Media.Image?</summary>

No. Close the ImageProxy CameraX gave you; closing the wrapped Media.Image directly breaks CameraX's image handling.
</details>

<details><summary>All four use cases always bind together?</summary>

No. Supported use-case combinations vary by device, resolution and configuration, so bind what the screen needs and handle unsupported combinations.
</details>

<!-- @after Use-Case Model :: visual -->
### One camera, separate jobs

<figure class="viz"><div class="viz-cols" style="--cols:4"><div class="node"><strong><code>Preview</code></strong><small>frames to the screen</small></div><div class="node"><strong><code>ImageCapture</code></strong><small>still photos, to memory or a file</small></div><div class="node"><strong><code>ImageAnalysis</code></strong><small>frames to your code for ML, scanning or measurement</small></div><div class="node"><strong><code>VideoCapture</code></strong><small>recording through the video API</small></div></div><figcaption>Each use case has its own output and its own failure. Bind only the ones a screen needs; supported combinations vary by device.</figcaption></figure>
